WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.292
Tool calling is easiest to understand with a concrete example.

00:00:04.292 --> 00:00:08.587
Suppose the user asks for the current weather in Greensboro.

00:00:08.587 --> 00:00:15.982
Instead of inventing an answer, the L L M can propose a structured call to a `get_weather` function with Greensboro as

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.486
the city argument.

00:00:19.006 --> 00:00:24.378
The application validates the request, executes the actual weather function,

00:00:24.378 --> 00:00:28.638
and receives structured data such as temperature and condition.

00:00:28.638 --> 00:00:34.773
That result can then be returned to the model so it can write a natural-language answer.

00:00:34.773 --> 00:00:39.035
The model proposes the call; the software performs it.
